# Downstream REST Error Mapping — TokenRealty

Human doc: [docs/rules/rest-client-errors.md](../../docs/rules/rest-client-errors.md).

## Required mapping

Every `RestClient.retrieve()` to another TokenRealty service or external API must map errors explicitly.

| Condition | Code / exception |
|-----------|------------------|
| 5xx or timeout (`ResourceAccessException`) | `{service}_unavailable` |
| 404 on resource lookup | `ResourceNotFoundException` or domain-specific not-found |
| Other 4xx | `{service}_error` or `ValidationException` |

Catch only `RestClientResponseException` and `ResourceAccessException` in client adapters — let domain exceptions propagate.

## Service name prefixes

| Downstream | Prefix | Example code |
|------------|--------|--------------|
| Property Registry | `property_registry_` | `property_registry_unavailable` |
| Token Issuance | `token_issuance_` | `token_issuance_unavailable` |
| Marketplace | `marketplace_` | `marketplace_unavailable` |
| Payment | `payment_` | `payment_unavailable` |

## Pattern

One `RestClient` `@Bean` per base URL in `*ClientConfig`. Client class wraps calls:

```java
@Component
public class TokenIssuanceClient {

    private final RestClient restClient;

    public TokenIssuanceClient(@Qualifier("tokenIssuanceRestClient") RestClient restClient) {
        this.restClient = restClient;
    }

    public ComplianceCheckResponse checkWallet(String walletAddress) {
        try {
            return restClient.get()
                    .uri("/v1/compliance/check/{walletAddress}", walletAddress)
                    .retrieve()
                    .body(ComplianceCheckResponse.class);
        } catch (RestClientResponseException ex) {
            if (ex.getStatusCode().is5xxServerError()) {
                throw new ValidationException("Token Issuance service unavailable");
            }
            throw new ValidationException("Compliance check failed: " + ex.getStatusText());
        } catch (ResourceAccessException ex) {
            throw new ValidationException("Token Issuance service unavailable");
        }
    }
}
```

Extract package-private `*ClientErrors` helper when a service has 3+ outbound clients.

## Rules

* No silent failures — no empty `catch (Exception)` that returns null
* Do not use broad `catch (Exception)` for business logic
* Propagate `Authorization` or service-account token when Auth Service exists
* Propagate `X-Trace-Id` (or `traceId`) on outbound calls
* Timeouts configured on `RestClient.Builder` — do not rely on defaults for financial paths
* Retries: only for idempotent GET; never auto-retry POST without idempotency key

